sections.body:
**1.** And the Savior will [disclose] to them [the word] that imparts life to the [All].

**2.** And those in [heaven], those on the earth, and those under the earth spoke the word [...].

**3.** [... which] will come to pass by his name.

**4.** (What is more), they will say concerning him:

**5.** “He was not born,” even though he was (in fact) born;

**6.** “he does not eat,” even though (in fact) he does eat;

**7.** “he does not drink,” even though (in fact) he does drink;

**8.** “he is uncircumcised,” even though he was (in fact) circumcised;

**9.** “he lacks true flesh,” even though he (in fact) came in flesh;

**10.** “he did not suffer death,” (even though) he did (in fact) experience suffering;

**11.** “he did not rise from among the dead,” (even though) he did (in fact) rise from among the dead.

**12.** All the [tribes, however], and all [the peoples] will speak [the truth], those who obtain the completed hope and the [gifts of] life from [you], O holy high priest [Melchize]d[ek].
